---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHeader num="10" title="Background" sub="Design Origins" />
    <div class="max-w-[720px]">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5 text-foreground-secondary">
        Every product ships with a default look: gray, flat, inconsistent. The structure was hard to scan, the palette felt borrowed, and nothing about the surface made you want to keep reading. So we started fixing the typography, the palette, the spacing, one token at a time, until the interface became a surface we actually enjoyed.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5 text-foreground-secondary">
        We needed a system that could travel across products — from landing pages to documentation portals to data dashboards — without losing coherence. That process added neutral grays, a single accent flow, and a tighter editorial rhythm. It kept growing until it covered every surface we regularly ship.
      </p>
      <div class="p-5 border-l-[3px] rounded-r-lg border-l-brand-accent bg-surface-subtle">
        <p class="text-sm italic text-foreground-secondary">Beauty emerges from constraints, not from addition. Every token earns its place.</p>
        <cite class="block mt-2 text-xs not-italic text-foreground-tertiary">&mdash; Blueprint Design Principles</cite>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
